"""The ChipLoom starter bank: sounds generated by ChipLoom recipes, so a new user can compose at once.

`build(path)` writes an ordinary sample bank (see `sample_library`) from the recipes below: drums, basses,
leads, chord and arpeggio waves, plucks, pads, textures and effects, each with a readable name, its role and
tags. Nothing is downloaded and no third-party sample is involved, so there is no rights question. The recipes
are deterministic (same bytes on every machine) and every pitched sound is tuned so that written C sounds C
(basses an octave lower), so any mix of entries plays in tune. A few palettes (`PAL-0001` ...) group entries
that work together. The bank is built on demand, by default under the ChipLoom home
(`sample_intake.starter_path()`), and becomes the active bank when no other bank was chosen.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

